  "policy": {
   "nbp_reference": 4.0,
   "next_mpc_label": "MPC next: 3-4 Mar",
   "pricing_text": "FRAs at the 12 Feb close (1x4 3.72, 3x6 3.46, 6x9 3.33, 9x12 3.31 vs WIBOR 3M 3.87) price roughly 55bp of NBP cuts within 12 months. The MPC held at 4.00% on 4 Feb; the statement says CPI may fall in Q1 and stay consistent with the target in coming quarters. Glapiński (5 Feb): a March cut if the projection shows nothing worrying; 3.5% possible as the end-point. Kotecki (12 Feb): March 'a very good moment' for -25bp, April possibly another; Masłowska also sees March.",
   "risk_text": "A March cut is the consensus: the risks are the mid-March CPI basket revision, strong wages (Q4 +8.5%) and fiscal slippage; abroad, Iran/oil and US tariffs move the long end."
  },
  "macro": {
   "cpi": {
    "v": 2.4,
    "m": "Dec final (GUS, 15 Jan); core 2.7%"
   },
   "projection_text": "NBP November 2025 projection: CPI 2.9% (2026), 2.5% (2027); the March 2026 projection comes with the 3-4 Mar MPC.",
   "fiscal_text": "2025 general-government deficit ~7.0% of GDP; 2026 budget deficit cap PLN 271.7bn (in force; at the Constitutional Tribunal for follow-up review), gross borrowing needs ~PLN 690bn.",
   "fiscal_risk_text": "2026 needs ~33% (11 Feb) financed; budget accounts PLN 183bn at end-January; Fitch reviews Poland on 27 Feb (after the close) and Moody's on 20 Mar, both with negative outlooks.",
   "backdrop_text": "The NBP held at 4.00% on 14 Jan and 4 Feb; December CPI 2.4% y/y (final), core 2.7%; 2025 GDP grew 3.6% (30 Jan); Q4 +4.0% y/y (12 Feb). Ratings: Fitch A- negative, Moody's A2 negative, S&P A- stable. 12 Feb: Q4 GDP +4.0% y/y (in line); Kotecki called March 'a very good moment' for -25bp and Masłowska also sees a March cut; BGK sold PLN 3.4bn of FPC (demand 6.3bn) plus 0.75bn; Millennium says above-potential growth limits the room for cuts. Abroad: Hungarian CPI 2.1% (2.4% expected); UK Q4 GDP +0.1%; US equities -1.6%, Bund 2.78%."
  },
  "calendar": {
   "plan_text": "MoF February plan (30 Jan): sale auctions on 11, 18 and 25 Feb (PLN 7-12bn each), no switch auction, a 33-week T-bill auction on 6 Feb; January sales were ~PLN 41.6bn incl. additional sales. BGK placed PLN 1bn of FWA0931 (Armed Forces Support Fund) privately (29-30 Jan). JPY 211.6bn priced on 6 Feb (3Y 1.88%, 5Y 2.22%, 10Y 2.90%, 20Y 3.65%); 33-week T-bills PLN 2.6bn at 3.529%. 11 Feb: PLN 11.9bn sold vs 25.8bn demand (cover 2.18) plus 1.38bn additional; OK0128 unsold; stop yields PS0131 4.298%, DS1033 4.732%, DS1035 5.035%, WS0437 5.148%.",
   "timing_text": "Within each auction week of the Aug 2025-Feb 2026 sample, yields drifted lower into the auction and the auction-day close was the cheapest point relative to the preceding session, so new buying is best executed at the auction-day close (18 and 25 Feb). February covers so far: 2.18x (11 Feb). The 3-4 Mar MPC with the new projection is the next event; a 25bp cut is the consensus.",
